.TH LUS-DOC 1 "" "Lus" "Lus Manual"
.SH NAME
lus-doc \- generate API documentation from doc comments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBlus doc\fR [\-o DIR] [\-\-format md|json|html] file ...
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generates reference documentation from the \fB\-\-\-\fR doc comments of each file.
Each file is one module.
Documentation describes the comments.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o DIR\fR
Write one file per module into \fBDIR\fR.
Without it, the output goes to standard output.
.TP
\fB\-\-format md|json|html\fR
Choose Markdown, the default, JSON, or HTML.
HTML needs \fB\-o\fR and adds an index and a search box, with links between entries.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
The documentation was written.
.TP
1
A file does not parse.
.TP
2
An option is malformed or a file cannot be read or written.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lus (1)
.PP
The CLI page of the Lus manual, https://lus.dev/manual/cli#lus-doc, has the same text with links to the rest of the manual.
